    "body": "Fixes #56443.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe memory-profiling dummy run can hand-build max_num_seqs requests without applying the scheduler's speculative query-token budget. For DSpark/DFlash, each request can require num_query_per_req draft query rows.\nFor example, with max_num_seqs=512, max_num_batched_tokens=2048, and DSpark K=5, the profiling path asks the speculator for 512 * 5 = 2560 query rows while its input buffers are sized for 2048 rows, so DSpark can read _anchor_idx past input_ids and later surface CUDA IndexKernel/device-side assert errors.\n\n## Changes\nCap the initial dummy/profile draft-generation pass to the largest complete set of query blocks that fits the speculator input buffer, preserve the full target-context and sampler projection for memory profiling, and fail early with a clear ValueError if a real query batch exceeds the input buffer.\n\nOther profiling dummy runs, including FlashInfer autotune, build target attention metadata and cannot use the initial skip-attention shortcut. Add a default no-op speculator hook that lets DFlash-family speculators cap the dummy request count before GPUModelRunner builds those synthetic batches. This does not affect real serving requests or other speculator implementations.\n\n## Existing PRs\n\n#53970 addresses the same `max_num_seqs * parallel-draft query width > max_num_batched_tokens` failure condition with a broader capacity-based fix: it raises `max_num_batched_tokens` to cover the worst-case parallel-draft batch and enlarges the DFlash input buffers. This PR instead leaves the configured target token budget unchanged and caps only synthetic profiling batches to the existing speculator capacity. It covers both the initial skip-attention memory profile and full-attention profiling dummy runs such as FlashInfer autotune, and adds a fail-fast check if a real serving batch violates the scheduler invariant already established by #51256. The approaches are alternatives for the startup crash, but differ in scope and memory/scheduling impact.\n\n#53080 separates target and draft scheduler budgets, but it does not constrain model-runner-generated profiling batches that bypass normal scheduler admission. #53577 covers broader DSpark/PP and padded graph safety work, but it has no matching profile query-buffer cap. #55133 and #56387 address different DSpark failure modes.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n### Common Configuration\n\n- Hardware: 4x NVIDIA H20\n- Tensor parallel size: 4\n- Image: `vllm/vllm-openai:deepseekv41-flash-0909`\n- CUDA graph mode: `FULL_AND_PIECEWISE`\n\n### DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash\n\n```bash\nvllm serve /data00/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 8000 \\\n  --served-model-name deepseek-v4.1-flash \\\n  --tokenizer-mode deepseek_v41 \\\n  --reasoning-parser deepseek_v41 \\\n  --tool-call-parser deepseek_v41 \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\n  --enable-expert-parallel \\\n  --max-model-len 262144 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 2048 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 512 \\\n  --block-size 64 \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.95 \\\n  --moe-backend auto \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE\",\"custom_ops\":[\"all\"]}' \\\n  --enable-auto-tool-choice \\\n  --enable-chunked-prefill \\\n  --enable-prefix-caching \\\n  --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dspark\",\"draft_sample_method\":\"greedy\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5}' \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --disable-uvicorn-access-log\n```\n\n### Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2\n\nFlashInfer autotune was left enabled by default.\n\n```bash\nvllm serve /data00/models/Qwen3.8-27B \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 8001 \\\n  --served-model-name qwen3.8-27b \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\n  --max-model-len 8192 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 512 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 128 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE\",\"custom_ops\":[\"all\"]}' \\\n  --enable-chunked-prefill \\\n  --enable-prefix-caching \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"model\":\"/data00/models/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":7}' \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --disable-uvicorn-access-log\n```\n\n### Qwen3-8B + DFlash\n\nFlashInfer autotune was left enabled by default.\n\n```bash\nvllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 8001 \\\n  --served-model-name qwen3-8b \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\n  --max-model-len 8192 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 512 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 64 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE\",\"custom_ops\":[\"all\"]}' \\\n  --enable-chunked-prefill \\\n  --enable-prefix-caching \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"model\":\"z-lab/Qwen3-8B-DFlash-b16\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":16}' \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --disable-uvicorn-access-log\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n### DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash\n\nWithout this PR, startup fails during memory profiling before the API server becomes ready:\n\n```text\n/__w/pytorch/pytorch/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/IndexKernel.cu:111: operator(): block: [0,0,0], thread: [...] Assertion `-sizes[i] <= index && index < sizes[i] && \"index out of bounds\"` failed.\nRuntimeError: CUDA error: CUBLAS_STATUS_EXECUTION_FAILED when calling `cublasGemmEx(...)`\nEngineCore failed to start.\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: device-side assert triggered\n```\n\nWith this PR, the service completed profiling, KV cache creation, CUDA graph capture, and API startup. `/health`, `/v1/models`, and two `/v1/completions` requests succeeded. The pod remained running with restart count 0, and the logs contained none of the failure signatures above.\n\n### Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2\n\nWithout this PR, startup fails during the initial memory profile. DFlash2 tries to process 128 requests with query width 8, requiring 1024 query rows while its input buffer contains only 512 rows. The logs show:\n\n```text\nIndexKernel.cu:111: Assertion `... index out of bounds` failed.\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: device-side assert triggered\nEngineCore failed to start.\n```\n\nWith this PR, both the initial memory profile and the default FlashInfer autotune completed, followed by KV cache creation, target/DFlash2 CUDA graph capture, and API startup. `/health`, `/v1/models`, and two `/v1/completions` requests succeeded. A 128-concurrency run completed 128/128 requests and generated 2812 completion tokens. The pod remained running with restart count 0, and the startup/request logs contained no CUDA, EngineCore, traceback, `ValueError`, or HTTP 500 failure signatures.\n\n### Qwen3-8B + DFlash\n\nWithout this PR, the initial memory-profile phase completes, but the default FlashInfer autotune dummy run uses 64 requests with query width 17, requiring 1088 query rows while the input buffer contains only 512 rows. The workers fail with:\n\n```text\nCUDA error (.../flash_fwd_launch_template.h:199): an illegal memory access was encountered\nEngineCore failed to start.\n```\n\nWith this PR, the initial profile, default FlashInfer autotune, KV cache creation, target/DFlash CUDA graph capture, and API startup all completed. `/health`, `/v1/models`, and two `/v1/completions` requests succeeded. A 64-concurrency run completed 64/64 requests and generated 2048 completion tokens. The pod remained running with restart count 0, and the startup/request logs contained no CUDA, EngineCore, traceback, `ValueError`, or HTTP 500 failure signatures.\n\n",
